Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tech Notes", "TechNotesSection",
 CellID->446237050,ExpressionUUID->"4357666d-36a3-4abf-9b9b-42e00764ce90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumStateEstimate", "[", 
   StyleBox["\[Ellipsis]", "TR"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "20e3d220-d0ab-41a2-8a84-9974a0032a17"],
 " uses measurement results to estimate properties of the preparation, \
including the system's quantum state. It checks if the measurements provided \
form a complete set for quantum state reconstruction, and then it performs \
maximum likelihood state estimation, and returns a Bayesian sampling \
function. The sampling function generates quantum states distributed \
according to the measurement results, with a prior given by the Bures metric. \
 Under the hood, it uses a Metropolis-Hastings algorithm where the random \
walk is implemented with matrix operations, rather than the usual random \
steps. The sampled states can be used to get Bayesian distributions of any \
parameters of the measured system. This includes the Bayesian mean quantum \
state. "
}], "Tutorials",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8873084637222033`*^9, 3.887308472678753*^9}, 
   3.887308629129823*^9},
 CellID->50414184,ExpressionUUID->"da0b60da-a378-4da8-af5c-51c9728d8c79"]
}, Open  ]],

